### Page 1 of 13

```text
Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins
Page 1 of 1
July 2, 2024

X:\Department Folders\Development Projects\2024\Brakes Plus Service Center PUDC-24-66\9_MISCELLANEOUS\Council Docs\Final\BrakesPlus_Agenda Memo.docx

MEMO

TO:

Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins, City of Cheyenne

City Council Members

FROM:
Cassie L. Pickett, PE, Engineering Manager

DATE:
July 02, 2024

SUBJECT:
Brakes Plus - Improvement Agreement for Pedestrian Connectivity
Improvements In-Lieu of Right-Of-Way Improvements

Purpose of Project:
This project is the private development of land located near the southeast corner of Ridge Road and
Gregg Way for the purpose of a Brakes Plus.

Reason for Contract:
This agreement was the result of the Brakes Plus Development providing a more practical public
improvement of pedestrian connectivity for the area rather than half of the right-of-way for Gregg
Way through the extents of the property. This is represented within the referenced agreement.

Estimated Cost:
The agreement outlines the details of the contract representing an exchange of improvements,
noting a comparable cost associated, and requiring no additional cash-in-lieu.  No funding source
necessary.

The Engineer’s Department has reviewed the request and respectfully recommends approval of the
requested Public Improvements Agreement.

CITY ENGINEER’S OFFICE
2101 O’Neil Avenue
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001
```

### Page 2 of 13

```text
Improvements Agreement
Page 1 of 5
City Contract # ________
IMPROVEMENT AGREEMENT

THIS AGREEMENT made and entered into this _____ of July, 2024, by and between (the
"Owner"), Brakes Plus, LLC (not WY) (the "Holder of a Deed of Trust"), and the CITY OF
CHEYENNE, STATE OF WYOMING, a body politic and corporate (the "City").

WITNESSETH:

WHEREAS, the Owner has made proper application and supporting document(s) for
request (Exemption from Platting or Site Development Plan), Engineering Plan Review Number
PUDC-24-66(the "Case") for the property described in the Case (the "Property");

WHEREAS, as a condition of approval of the Case, the Owner is obligated to enter into an
agreement with the City that provides that the Owner shall either construct certain public
improvements as established in the City of Cheyenne Municipal Code and Unified Development
Code and which area is set forth on Exhibit A attached hereto and incorporated herein
(collectively, the "Requirement Area”) or provide a Cash-in-Lieu Payments of the same (the
"Guarantee");

WHEREAS, the term "Cash-In-Lieu" (the "CIL") shall mean those payments made by
Owner in advance pursuant to UDC Sections 4.1.5.b.6 and 4.1.5.b.7 to satisfy in full Owner's,
Holder of a Deed of Trust, or the Owner obligations with respect to certain specified Public
Improvements as set forth herein.

WHEREAS, the Property is 1) uniquely situated and encumbered both by its orientation to
and intention to be served by access(es) internal to the shopping center complex; 2) also fronts on
an existing, minimally improved public Right-of-Way primarily serving as a secondary access to
an unincorporated single-family residential neighborhood, and 3) provides an opportunity to make
necessary public pedestrian connections in an existing developed block where no reasonable such
connection currently exists;

WHEREAS, as a condition of approval of the Case, the Owner is providing certain
alternative improvements to protect and serve the public interest as set forth on Exhibit B attached
hereto and incorporated herein (collectively, the "Improvements");

WHEREAS, Cash In Lieu Amounts and Financial Security for Public Improvements.
Upon the City’s acceptance of Owner’s construction of the Improvements by a Certificate of
Compliance ("COC"); Owner's proportionate fair share of Public Improvements in accordance
with UDC Sections 4.1.5.b.6 and 4.1.5.b.7 which payment amounts (the "Cash in Lieu
Amounts") shall be as specified as calculated per the Requirement Area on Exhibit A,
Owner’s financial responsibility for such scheduled Public Improvements shall be deemed
permanently satisfied with respect to construction on the Property;

WHEREAS, The Parties agree to the installation of those Public Improvements,
associated cost estimates and fee schedules, and dedications, easements, payments or
12:17 pm, Jul 03 2024
