### Page 4 of 13

```text
Improvements Agreement
Page 3 of 5
as part of the Case that must be completed by the Owner prior to the issuance of a Certificate of
Occupancy, including, without limitation the satisfactory completion of the Improvements or the
posting of a Guarantee, or cash-in-lieu for such completion.

4.
The Owner and Holder of a Deed of Trust hereby consent and authorize the City
to enter onto the Property to construct, install, maintain, and/or replace all or any portion of the
Improvements required by the Case. No Guarantee will be accepted for Improvements that lie
outside of the Property unless the property owner grants an acceptable easement to the City. Owner
and the Holder of a Deed of Trust hereby unconditionally waive and release the City from any and
all claims or other legal liability that arise out of or are attributable to constructing, installing,
maintaining and/or replacing the Improvements. This consent, waiver and release extends to the
City and all its officials, attorneys, agents, employees, and contractors of a landscaping or
construction firm.

5.
The Holder of a Deed of Trust hereby consents to the imposition of the restriction
on conveyance, sale, or transfer as set forth above, as well as all other notes and restrictions set
forth on the face of the mylar or any supporting document(s). The Holder of a Deed of Trust, if
any, further agrees that in the event it acquires title or control over the disposition of all or any
portion of the Property, whether through foreclosure or otherwise, it will comply with the terms of
the restriction of sale and other such notes and restrictions.

6.
The City and any purchaser of all or any portion of the Property shall have the
authority to bring an action to compel the enforcement of this Agreement, including the restriction
on sale contained herein. Such authority shall include the right to compel rescission of any sale,
conveyance or transfer of any such Property contrary to the provisions this Agreement.

7.
This Agreement may be amended from time to time by a written instrument signed
by all parties hereto.

8.
This Agreement and all restrictions contained herein shall run with the land and
shall extend to and be binding upon all successors, assigns, heirs, and personal representatives of
all or any portion of the Property.

9.
The parties hereby stipulate and represent that all procedures necessary to
authorize the execution of this Agreement have been performed and that the persons signing for
each of the parties have been authorized to do so.

REMAINDER OF PAGE INTENTIONALLY BLANK
