Base Information. Base information provided by Steil Surveying Services, LLC.
Zoning. Site is currently zoned MUB - Mixed-Use Business-Emphasis; this Site Design assumes
conformance with City approval of a Re-zoning application to CB - Community Business.
Ownership and Maintenance. Site improvements shown on this drawing are to be owned and
maintained by the owner and/or assigns.
Architecture. Building footprint and Trash Enclosure per ARCODEV Architects, P.C., 2024.
See Building Elevations for compliance with UDC Section 6.9.
Grading, Drainage, and Utilities. Proposed layout/design(s) to be reviewed and finalized by Lovas
Engineering, P.C. and may be adjusted during the construction permitting and Engineering Plan
Review (EPR) process following approval of this Site Plan without necessitating its revision. Refer to
Building Mechanical drawings for wet utility services entering buildings.
Signage. A minimum of one ground-mounted commercial sign will be required for business
identification. Commercial signage review and approval is not part of this site plan application and shall
be deferred to separate sign pennit(s) at such time that design is completed. Incidental and directional
signs, (i.e. "no parking," "private drive," etc.) may be installed without amending this Site Plan.
Any building-mounted wall signage will be proposed through separate application(s).
Parking and Circulation. Vehicle parking and Circulation shown on this Site Plan is for the use of
customers, employees, guests, invitees, and Delivery and Service Providers. (Asphalt surfacing may
be changed to concrete at owners option without amending this plan)
Lighting. All building and pole mounted lighting shall conform to applicable code section(s).
Applicant requests that lighting review be deferred to coincide with the building permit application.
Parking: Parking is reserved for employees and patrons. Up to five (5) parking spaces may be signed
as "Reserved" or "Employees Only" at Owner discretion without amending this plan.
Trash Vehicle Access: Trash vehicles may enter the property from Bluegrass Circle, drive east past
the trash enclosure, back up into the drive-through lane, access the trash enclosure for front-loader use,
back up into the drive-through lane, and exit the property facing forward to Bluegrass Circle.
Open Space Approach
Per UDC §6.9.3, Open Space is required at 5% of the combined building footprint (±4,900 SF) for a
minimum of 245 SF. An outdoor plaza area is proposed at the southwest corner of the building.
Outdoor furniture, seating, and/or decorative paving may be used to define the space at the Owner's
discretion. Other amenities within the plaza area may be installed without amending this Site Plan .
