BRAKES PLUS - 1101
PAGE 1
LOVAS ENGINEERING, PC   |   1869 GRIZZLY GULCH, CHEYENNE, WY  82009   |   chris@lovasengineering.com
Mrs.
Cassie Pickett, P.E. – Senior Staff Engineer
City of Cheyenne Engineering Department
Via:
City of Cheyenne OpenGov Platform
BRAKES PLUS – GREGG WAY ROW – ENGINEER’S COST OPINION (PUDC-24-66)
6/24/2024
Dear Mrs. Pickett,
In response to request from City Engineering department, below is a list of bid items and associated probable
construction costs related to civil infrastructure improvements within Gregg Way ROW adjacent to the Brakes
Plus Project.
*It should be noted that opinions of probable construction costs rendered by Engineer represent our reasonable
professional engineering opinion and furnished for general guidance.  Engineer makes no representation,
warranty, or guarantee, expressed nor implied, as to the accuracy of such opinions as compared to bid or actual
costs.
The estimated quantities for infrastructure are based upon site plan currently under review.  Lovas Engineering,
PC opinion of approximate construction costs have been derived using the following assumed key parameters:
•
387 SY 6” asphalt over 8” grading ‘W’ (3” grading ‘A’ / 3” grading ‘D’)
•
188 LF type ‘A’ curb & gutter
•
130 CY unclassified excavation
•
188 LF 5’ wide 4” depth concrete sidewalk over 4” grading ‘W’
The estimate also includes estimated contractor fees such as bonds/insurance, mobilization, potholing utilities,
force account, traffic control, stormwater management and construction management.  The estimate is based on
present value and does not account for inflation in construction materials or labor costs.  The estimate does not
include engineering, planning or consulting fees.
Engineer’s Opinion of Approximate Construction Costs:
$49,900.00
150% = $74,850.00
If you have any questions or require additional information, please feel free to contact me directly.
Respectfully Submitted,
Christofer S. Lovas, PE | Lovas Engineering, PC
